systars is a modern reimplementation of SYSTARS, a CAD tool for the synthesis
and analysis of VLSI systolic/wavefront arrays (E. T. L. Omtzigt, Delft
University of Technology, 1988). See docs/architecture/lineage.md for the
methods it builds on and their references.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Gemmini
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

systars began as a Python plan modelled on Gemmini
(https://github.com/ucb-bar/gemmini), and parts of its design follow Gemmini:
the execute command set (CONFIG, PRELOAD, COMPUTE, COMPUTE_ACCUMULATE), the
local address encoding (src/systars/memory/local_addr.py) and the accumulator
(src/systars/memory/accumulator.py). Gemmini's copyright notice and license
follow.

